course: dictionary
lesson: 5276
title: Judgement: thinking it through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A judgement is an opinion or decision you reach after thinking carefully about something. Adults say «use your judgement» when they want you to think sensibly and decide well for yourself. Good judgement means making sensible choices.
explain: Look at the context clue: «a fair judgement looks at what someone actually said and did.» A fair judgement needs real evidence, so it is not a guess or a rumour. «Everyone knows» is not proof, so a judgement built only on it is weak.
explain: In a court, a judgement is the official decision of a judge. In religion, the Day of Judgement is the time when Christians believe God will judge all people. Each meaning is still about deciding after weighing things up.
fact: Judgement means the ability to make good, sensible decisions.
fact: A judgement can also be an opinion you form after thinking about something.
fact: In a court, a judgement is the official decision of a judge or court.
fact: The Day of Judgement is when, Christians believe, God will judge all people at the end of time.
fact: A «snap judgement» is a decision made very quickly, without much thought.
exercise: Safety teachers say «use your judgement» on the way home. What does this ask you to do? | Wait for someone else to decide | Copy whatever everyone else does | *Think sensibly and make a good decision | Run as fast as you can without thinking
exercise: «A fair judgement looks at what someone actually said and did.» Which judgement is fair? | A snap judgement made without looking | Based on «everyone knows» | Based on not liking their name | *Based on what a person really said and did
exercise: In a court, who makes the official judgement? | *A judge | A passing bus driver | A friend of the family | A shop owner
test: Ben says he made a snap judgement that the film was bad after five minutes. What does snap judgement mean? | *A decision made very quickly, without much thought | A court's official ruling | A decision made after a whole week of thinking | A decision about the weather
test: What is the Day of Judgement? | A day for judging cakes at a fair | A school sports day | A court holiday | *The time, Christians believe, when God will judge all people
exam: Which choice best shows good judgement? | Making a choice just because it is the quickest | Deciding only on what your friend says | Crossing the road without looking | *Thinking carefully about the choice and deciding sensibly
